# `--no-odr-check` and `--odr-stats` (mortar's; spec/cli.md §3.9,
# spec/odr.md O-41):
# - `--no-odr-check` is `--odr=off`: the program of k5-vtable-size.test
#   (a class with different virtual functions in a.o and b.o), which
#   mortar reports by default (`odr-size-mismatch`, a warning), links
#   with no diagnostic and runs. The check never changes the output, so
#   the bytes are those of the default link (checked by hand; that link
#   is not made here, because its warning would fail this test, which
#   names no `diag`).
# - `--odr-stats` prints one line of statistics on standard error, with
#   the mode (`off` under `--no-odr-check`, `warn` by default) and the
#   findings (none on the legal program main.o a.o).
# The references know neither option and link the line plainly.
# It lives in diag/, not odr/: the producers lane (WP-099) re-links the
# odr/ corpus with hod's objects and compares the standard error, which
# `--odr-stats` makes differ by its time.
#@ spec: odr.md "§8.1"
#@ requires: g++

cxx -O0 a.cc -o a.o
cxx -O0 b.cc -o b.o
cxx -O0 main.cc -o main.o
cxx -O0 main-a.cc -o main-a.o
link(bfd,lld,mold) g++ -static main.o a.o b.o -o prog
link(mortar) g++ -static main.o a.o b.o -Wl,--no-odr-check -o prog
  no-diag: odr
run prog
  stdout: 1 1
link(mortar) g++ -static main.o a.o b.o -Wl,--no-odr-check -Wl,--odr-stats -o prog2
  diag: ^*: odr-stats: mode off; 
  no-diag: different sizes
link(mortar) g++ -static main-a.o a.o -Wl,--odr-stats -o legal
  diag: ^*: odr-stats: mode warn; 
  diag: findings W1 0, W2 0, W3 0, W4 0;
link(bfd,lld,mold) g++ -static main-a.o a.o -o legal
run legal
  stdout: 1
check(mortar) cmp prog2 prog
  has: ^identical$

#--- a.cc
struct B {
  virtual int f() { return 1; }
  virtual int g() { return 2; }
  virtual ~B() {}
};
int from_a() { B b; B* p = &b; return p->f(); }
#--- b.cc
struct B {
  virtual int f() { return 1; }
  virtual ~B() {}
};
int from_b() { B b; B* p = &b; return p->f(); }
#--- main.cc
#include <cstdio>
int from_a();
int from_b();
int main() { std::printf("%d %d\n", from_a(), from_b()); }
#--- main-a.cc
#include <cstdio>
int from_a();
int main() { std::printf("%d\n", from_a()); }
